{"char_offset": [130, 164], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 4, "paragraph_text": "Hand sanitizer, essential medicine", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > p[4]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "bba0d007367342534fd88e408c7c3b9c9f7c4b4e5f9045a7673b183cb3088b92", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [165, 195], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 5, "paragraph_text": "Viruses, bacteria, antibiotics", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > p[5]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "d960413a8aada05d9c0370a3ffb916f5c0ec9dc7b02a373176851907fdec8c85", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [196, 392], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Hand sanitizers can be used often"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 6, "paragraph_text": "An alcohol-based sanitizer does not create antibiotic resistance. Unlike other antiseptics and antibiotics, pathogens (harmful germs) do not seem to develop resistance to alcohol-based sanitizers.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Hand sanitizers can be used often > p[6]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "5393ae3f18648a6a492d35d023aeb2301e4cacbe8893eb98394525784518665b", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [393, 757], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Alcohol-based sanitizers are safe for everyone to use"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 7, "paragraph_text": "Alcohols in the sanitizers have not been shown to create any relevant health issues. Little alcohol is absorbed into the skin, and most products contain an emollient to reduce skin dryness. Allergic contact dermatitis and bleaching of hand hair due to alcohol are very rare adverse effects. Accidental swallowing and intoxication have been described in rare cases.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Alcohol-based sanitizers are safe for everyone to use > p[7]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "44026c6dcc65ad88636486ae9a5e6e846b2afd5f4c3728529d641c7303485799", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [758, 917], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Alcohol-based sanitizers can be used in religions where alcohol is prohibited"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 8, "paragraph_text": "Any manufactured substance developed to alleviate illness or contribute to better health is permitted by the Qur'an, including alcohol used as a medical agent.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Alcohol-based sanitizers can be used in religions where alcohol is prohibited > p[8]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "64459494222fd5b881df7ae52640e3696ee118bad8e10115ffa905cb84996569", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [918, 1067], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: The amount of alcohol-based sanitizer you use matters"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 9, "paragraph_text": "Apply a palmful of alcohol-based sanitizer to cover all surfaces of your hands. Rub your hands together using the right technique until they are dry.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: The amount of alcohol-based sanitizer you use matters > p[9]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "f4f5a180ff27971d6e8bef8923db58dd4a8ff8652a874069e2c3a70f1ca68a79", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [1068, 1115], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: The amount of alcohol-based sanitizer you use matters"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 10, "paragraph_text": "The entire procedure should last 20-30 seconds.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: The amount of alcohol-based sanitizer you use matters > p[10]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "2f211d83d6a33b32eb8531d96f85afb4c8816a46f11bc435ac523d81d8b6f2c3", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [1116, 1332], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: It is safer to frequently clean your hands and not wear gloves"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 11, "paragraph_text": "Wearing gloves risks transferring germs from one surface to another and contaminating your hands when removing them. Wearing gloves does not replace cleaning hands. Health workers wear gloves only for specific tasks.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: It is safer to frequently clean your hands and not wear gloves > p[11]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "35eaebd4ae4bfe6e6f785e5d954d9466a44b593618d70f372011dcdd9c874c15", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [1333, 1602], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Touching a communal bottle of alcohol-based sanitizer will not infect you"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 12, "paragraph_text": "Once you've sanitized your hands, you have disinfected them from any germs that may have been on the bottle. If everyone uses sanitizer in a public place such as a supermarket entrance, the risk of germs on communal items will be lower and will help keep everyone safe.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Touching a communal bottle of alcohol-based sanitizer will not infect you > p[12]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "722faae3cd6f5cf797a02a839019e906b1318fdd193d8bd9adeb9f46949376e6", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [1603, 1761], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: An alcohol-based handrub is listed as a WHO essential medicine"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 13, "paragraph_text": "Clean hands protect patients, health workers, other caregivers and everyone from infection. Cleaning your hands is one of the key measures to prevent disease.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: An alcohol-based handrub is listed as a WHO essential medicine > p[13]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "77d53f67a4989bfd0864e319b2170a2ffa9b45f845a4a64c8f80629f65c27e51", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [1762, 2031], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Vitamin and mineral supplements cannot cure COVID-19"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 14, "paragraph_text": "Micronutrients, such as vitamins D and C and zinc, are critical for a well-functioning immune system and play a vital role in promoting health and nutritional well-being. There is currently no guidance on the use of micronutrient supplements as a treatment of COVID-19.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Vitamin and mineral supplements cannot cure COVID-19 > p[14]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "ba6d5d163b51a94a78143709679b0c46de44da764ec5f62d9e0699afe0b4a4fd", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [2032, 2112], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Vitamin and mineral supplements cannot cure COVID-19"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 15, "paragraph_text": "WHO is coordinating efforts to develop and evaluate medicines to treat COVID-19.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Vitamin and mineral supplements cannot cure COVID-19 > p[15]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "ed82bc94dc306d27a316a6ad00527a9e0b6b1d1e4bef2409dd5add9155676c92", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [2113, 2205], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "Is dexamethasone a treatment for all COVID-19 patients?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 16, "paragraph_text": "Dexamethasone should be reserved for patients who need it most. It should not be stockpiled.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > Is dexamethasone a treatment for all COVID-19 patients? > p[16]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "a9fe5b2901b610673c4da0d55a9cc6818e65cdf00f402310457d8be3e493d408", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [2206, 2473], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "Is dexamethasone a treatment for all COVID-19 patients?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 17, "paragraph_text": "It provided no improvement for patients with mild symptoms. Dexamethasone is a corticosteroid used for its anti-inflammatory and immunosuppressive effects. For some COVID-19 patients on ventilators, a daily 6 mg dose of dexamethasone for 10 days improved their health", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > Is dexamethasone a treatment for all COVID-19 patients? > p[17]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "3654281c88737d5a4e09859bcc679fb2b37acd2f7727df02c96ecd5f3969fcc1", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [2474, 2638], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "Fact: Water or swimming does not transmit the COVID-19 virus"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 18, "paragraph_text": "The COVID-19 virus does not transmit through water while swimming. However, the virus spreads between people when someone has close contact with an infected person.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > Fact: Water or swimming does not transmit the COVID-19 virus > p[18]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "08add21b3f484104ac4239ff1cbab61131796d7ae6c33e5fdc1d1cb2be44e893", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [2639, 2937], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "Fact: Water or swimming does not transmit the COVID-19 virus"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 19, "paragraph_text": "Avoid crowds and maintain at least a 1-metre distance from others, even when you are swimming or at swimming areas. Wear a mask when you’re not in the water and you can’t stay distant. Clean your hands frequently, cover a cough or sneeze with a tissue or bent elbow, and stay home if you’re unwell.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > Fact: Water or swimming does not transmit the COVID-19 virus > p[19]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "0f2ff57bc8284967d51221da8c10173dcf0bd6c407c105abdfb63579653c2e81", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [2938, 3290], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: The likelihood of shoes spreading COVID-19 is very low"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 20, "paragraph_text": "The likelihood of COVID-19 being spread on shoes and infecting individuals is very low. As a precautionary measure, particularly in homes where infants and small children crawl or play on floors, consider leaving your shoes at the entrance of your home. This will help prevent contact with dirt or any waste that could be carried on the soles of shoes.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: The likelihood of shoes spreading COVID-19 is very low > p[20]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "55e102f181e440a15d10bfb92c29a2a2604cdd8982a2fce153641329604032d6", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [3291, 3410], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: The coronavirus disease (COVID-19) is caused by a virus, NOT by bacteria"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 21, "paragraph_text": "The virus that causes COVID-19 is in a family of viruses called Coronaviridae. Antibiotics do not work against viruses.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: The coronavirus disease (COVID-19) is caused by a virus, NOT by bacteria > p[21]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "e3bc3092119e1fed2ea54058c2dedb5b1ecf67ed9e56400a76bf50643b09413f", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [3411, 3581], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: The coronavirus disease (COVID-19) is caused by a virus, NOT by bacteria"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 22, "paragraph_text": "Some people who become ill with COVID-19 can also develop a bacterial infection as a complication. In this case, antibiotics may be recommended by a health care provider.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: The coronavirus disease (COVID-19) is caused by a virus, NOT by bacteria > p[22]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "b5a1b12ccbe5f7b8e3f876c04d149b673d6a60700bbe94ce11f1cee49f361e94", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [3582, 3730], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: The coronavirus disease (COVID-19) is caused by a virus, NOT by bacteria"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 23, "paragraph_text": "There is currently no licensed medication to cure COVID-19. If you have symptoms, call your health care provider or COVID-19 hotline for assistance.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: The coronavirus disease (COVID-19) is caused by a virus, NOT by bacteria > p[23]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "6b7a27a0507cd0de192135a67420116c2f0355b8240147dd9d2b5a6951461506", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [3731, 4053], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: The prolonged use of medical masks* when properly worn, DOES NOT cause CO2 intoxication nor oxygen deficiency"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 24, "paragraph_text": "The prolonged use of medical masks can be uncomfortable. However, it does not lead to CO2 intoxication nor oxygen deficiency. While wearing a medical mask, make sure it fits properly and that it is tight enough to allow you to breathe normally. Do not re-use a disposable mask and always change it as soon as it gets damp.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: The prolonged use of medical masks* when properly worn, DOES NOT cause CO2 intoxication nor oxygen deficiency > p[24]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "2601746b2f88e63213f9d4991e84ae9ae263bd2b5fdf450817eb2589e1013adb", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [4054, 4181], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: The prolonged use of medical masks* when properly worn, DOES NOT cause CO2 intoxication nor oxygen deficiency"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 25, "paragraph_text": "* Medical masks (also known as surgical masks) are flat or pleated; they are affixed to the head with straps or have ear loops.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: The prolonged use of medical masks* when properly worn, DOES NOT cause CO2 intoxication nor oxygen deficiency > p[25]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "f8094b9f29ac7dbb345543c376c10f04a07b6aff4e73af041ae3cd793a88e00b", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [4182, 4248], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Drinking alcohol does not protect you against COVID-19 and can be dangerous"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 26, "paragraph_text": "The harmful use of alcohol increases your risk of health problems.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Drinking alcohol does not protect you against COVID-19 and can be dangerous > p[26]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "5b062743193604189f9851b40bc140f145ac5e7215a6ff3d6ac7e10a649c3869", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [4249, 4612], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Adding pepper to your soup or other meals DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 27, "paragraph_text": "Hot peppers in your food, though very tasty, cannot prevent or cure COVID-19. The best way to protect yourself against the new coronavirus is to keep at least 1 metre away from others and to wash your hands frequently and thoroughly. It is also beneficial for your general health to maintain a balanced diet, stay well hydrated, exercise regularly and sleep well.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Adding pepper to your soup or other meals DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19 > p[27]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "db7343fb7520b2a9c0fe8936b8fe439d17ac96d8cab70ca722351481e4a70d70", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [4613, 4811], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Adding pepper to your soup or other meals DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19", "COVID-19: Adding pepper to your soup or other meals DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 28, "paragraph_text": "Do not under any circumstance spray or introduce bleach or any other disinfectant into your body. These substances can be poisonous if ingested and cause irritation and damage to your skin and eyes.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Adding pepper to your soup or other meals DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19 > COVID-19: Adding pepper to your soup or other meals DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19 > p[28]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "1f5e39149b9a38ecbdb874b6c7e93bdf16a31972c281414fc2f13ca6fbb0d93b", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [4812, 4973], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Adding pepper to your soup or other meals DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19", "COVID-19: Adding pepper to your soup or other meals DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 29, "paragraph_text": "Bleach and disinfectant should be used carefully to disinfect surfaces only. Remember to keep chlorine (bleach) and other disinfectants out of reach of children.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Adding pepper to your soup or other meals DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19 > COVID-19: Adding pepper to your soup or other meals DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19 > p[29]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "0ec791b90e2796a41829167e3d716b1d9b8dccd2023234aca1839d096c1f4fc0", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [4974, 5286], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Drinking methanol, ethanol or bleach DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19 and can be extremely dangerous"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 30, "paragraph_text": "Methanol, ethanol, and bleach are poisons. Drinking them can lead to disability and death. Methanol, ethanol, and bleach are sometimes used in cleaning products to kill the virus on surfaces – however you should never drink them. They will not kill the virus in your body and they will harm your internal organs.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Drinking methanol, ethanol or bleach DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19 and can be extremely dangerous > p[30]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "be930b8265263c410a16f8b030f3c376340895875b8dc5b2dd0abe668a26ecb4", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [5287, 5548], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Drinking methanol, ethanol or bleach DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19 and can be extremely dangerous"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 31, "paragraph_text": "To protect yourself against COVID-19, disinfect objects and surfaces, especially the ones you touch regularly. You can use diluted bleach or alcohol for that. Make sure you clean your hands frequently and thoroughly and avoid touching your eyes, mouth and nose.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Drinking methanol, ethanol or bleach DOES NOT prevent or cure COVID-19 and can be extremely dangerous > p[31]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "2990b3c832da3c61ba3f301de8719c38582f324de140b711b2000fc1c1cc453a", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [5549, 5800], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Exposing yourself to the sun or temperatures higher than 25°C DOES NOT protect you from COVID-19"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 32, "paragraph_text": "You can catch COVID-19, no matter how sunny or hot the weather is. Countries with hot weather have reported cases of COVID-19. To protect yourself, make sure you clean your hands frequently and thoroughly and avoid touching your eyes, mouth, and nose.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Exposing yourself to the sun or temperatures higher than 25°C DOES NOT protect you from COVID-19 > p[32]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "82efef9f2dec4bcf6c69de20c008dd92ae03f4557697f61009b0185c9538c633", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [5801, 6098], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: The COVID-19 virus can spread in hot and humid climates"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 33, "paragraph_text": "The best way to protect yourself against COVID-19 is by maintaining physical distance of at least 1 metre from others and frequently cleaning your hands. By doing this you eliminate viruses that may be on your hands and avoid infection that could occur by then touching your eyes, mouth, and nose.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: The COVID-19 virus can spread in hot and humid climates > p[33]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "0f21bc8a13e55d731c1748da88b12421172edcfdc2c84ea9e3b2cec67df9575f", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [6099, 6310], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Cold weather and snow CANNOT kill the COVID-19 virus"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 34, "paragraph_text": "There is no reason to believe that cold weather can kill the new coronavirus or other diseases. The normal human body temperature remains around 36.5°C to 37°C, regardless of the external temperature or weather.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Cold weather and snow CANNOT kill the COVID-19 virus > p[34]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "f7bedb96dc9dfa9affbb8ccf88fd99e9340c0b291e48dc214cd2c1c20ec41511", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [6311, 6628], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "The COVID-19 virus CANNOT be spread through mosquito bites"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 35, "paragraph_text": "To date there has been no information nor evidence to suggest that the new coronavirus could be transmitted by mosquitoes. The new coronavirus is a respiratory virus which spreads primarily through droplets generated when an infected person coughs or sneezes, or through droplets of saliva or discharge from the nose.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > The COVID-19 virus CANNOT be spread through mosquito bites > p[35]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "012103cfb44fc5edce85200f8534042f8a4ab7bd955cf82e0f653eb1e77ff29b", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [6629, 6906], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Hand dryers are NOT effective in killing the COVID-19 virus"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 36, "paragraph_text": "Hand dryers are not effective in killing the COVID-19 virus. To protect yourself, frequently clean your hands with an alcohol-based hand rub or wash them with soap and water. Once your hands are cleaned, you should dry them thoroughly by using paper towels or a warm air dryer.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Hand dryers are NOT effective in killing the COVID-19 virus > p[36]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "9d5baeaa26fd0c032fffc2179c70d9b46053a019a58b67bf6b3f6b8c6b197dc6", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [6907, 7144], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: People of all ages can be infected by the COVID-19 virus"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 37, "paragraph_text": "Older people and younger people can be infected by the COVID-19 virus. Older people, and people with pre-existing medical conditions such as asthma, diabetes, and heart disease are more vulnerable to becoming severely ill with the virus.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: People of all ages can be infected by the COVID-19 virus > p[37]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "27a9101d4cf4ea81cc4f0c2e84ad459f64e88d7fad96c81a337e44d9bb06455e", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [7145, 7300], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: People of all ages can be infected by the COVID-19 virus"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 38, "paragraph_text": "WHO advises people of all ages to take steps to protect themselves from the virus, for example by following good hand hygiene and good respiratory hygiene.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: People of all ages can be infected by the COVID-19 virus > p[38]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "ba234f4083f545a14a687c78e4e810033447c57b6277b9a4ad5988eb88d38f08", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [7301, 7353], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Antibiotics CANNOT prevent or treat COVID-19"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 39, "paragraph_text": "Antibiotics work only against bacteria, not viruses.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Antibiotics CANNOT prevent or treat COVID-19 > p[39]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "91f97351c5143f91c3fefbe79bda5102e123b1185d82ff51d5bd94497b33c077", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
{"char_offset": [7354, 7458], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:33Z", "heading_path": ["Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters", "FACT: Antibiotics CANNOT prevent or treat COVID-19"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 40, "paragraph_text": "COVID-19 is caused by a virus, and therefore antibiotics should not be used for prevention or treatment.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) advice for the public: Mythbusters > FACT: Antibiotics CANNOT prevent or treat COVID-19 > p[40]", "sha256_of_page": "d2cd31a347be2285e6aef482a9bacf4bd2870ba30f98834d62588fcc4f47bd05", "sha256_of_paragraph": "cc488429540c0a3e23086fb449a5e16b0eb020c9f808ab5d35096f0b431cd097", "source_id": "WHO-MYTH", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/emergencies/diseases/novel-coronavirus-2019/advice-for-public/myth-busters"}
