{"char_offset": [260, 396], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": [], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 5, "paragraph_text": "A lock ( ) or https:// means you've safely connected to the .gov website. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "p[5]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "08726f3b3f49204e598fe5732a5ae312265bd54974f09b6d68a2751b4420b501", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [397, 455], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Key points"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 6, "paragraph_text": "The common cold has no cure but should improve on its own.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Key points > p[6]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "cc98f01e28f7088f9ea04399cdd6be7c3757a3ea718c4f9847b1ea5409c3c920", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [456, 526], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Key points"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 7, "paragraph_text": "Antibiotics don't work against viruses and won't help you feel better.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Key points > p[7]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "83952f2ce2a489f78d4bc502e4cfedca7c105ec6e0f515be74f699258f266148", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [527, 779], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Key points"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 8, "paragraph_text": "If you have cold-like symptoms and suspect you have COVID-19 or flu, get tested, especially if you are at higher risk for severe illness. Antiviral treatments are available for COVID-19 and flu and work best when started very soon after symptoms begin.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Key points > p[8]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "54d95f38dea3068889aa6e939a55e73583db163c02f80dd2f37c57356345e14c", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [780, 1090], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Overview"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 9, "paragraph_text": "Most people with cold symptoms (runny nose, cough, sore throat) will not require specific treatment. They can take steps to manage their symptoms and prevent spreading the virus. However, there are rare cases when a viral infection can lead to a bacterial infection, like pneumonia, which requires antibiotics.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Overview > p[9]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "1b75dd16a81787da021b4066541449fb50c9746436ef4599059a3176582e48f9", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [1091, 1428], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Overview", "Fact"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 10, "paragraph_text": "If you don't need antibiotics, you shouldn't take them. They can cause side effects ranging from mild reactions, like a rash, to more serious health problems. Problems can include severe allergic reactions, antimicrobial-resistant infections, and C. diff infection. C. diff causes diarrhea that can lead to severe colon damage and death.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Overview > Fact > p[10]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "9e2fb15ff12c4c872ef35f14715fadb72652c756eef66fabc3b3ebae468561a6", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [1429, 1945], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Overview", "Fact"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 11, "paragraph_text": "If a healthcare provider diagnoses your illness as COVID-19 or flu, you may be eligible for antiviral treatment that can lessen symptoms and shorten the time you are sick. You should start COVID-19 treatment within 5-7 days after symptoms begin or within 2 days for flu treatment. Contact your healthcare provider promptly if you have symptoms and are at higher risk for complications from COVID-19 or flu. Treatment may reduce your risk of complications, including those that can result in hospitalization or death.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Overview > Fact > p[11]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "34b7b90bb7c14f6fdaa1af11f5c9c56d818233cad6b19bc50ef52246f8919366", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [1946, 2049], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Overview", "Fact"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 12, "paragraph_text": "There are currently no antivirals that work against other respiratory viruses that cause cold symptoms.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Overview > Fact > p[12]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "43510278b78fda7032b16d86e0267e8e13bd436c5b999dd524a5cc1741a4e242", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2050, 2123], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 13, "paragraph_text": "In most cases, your cold symptoms will get better on their own with time.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > p[13]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "acdd148a4e5e834c38d8881f83c885f68a1aae1e0b341112d0993c42ba000cd7", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2124, 2512], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms", "Adults"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 14, "paragraph_text": "Ask your healthcare provider or pharmacist about over-the-counter (OTC) medicines, such as pain relievers and fever reducers. These can lessen symptoms and help you feel better. Be sure to mention any other prescription or OTC medicines you are taking. Always use OTC medicines as directed. Remember, OTC medicines may provide temporary relief of symptoms, but will not cure your illness.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > Adults > p[14]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "06e0ce7757d261a121071f9532e8678379ea98be6f0c8daa800c1e6798bed650", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2513, 2824], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms", "Children"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 15, "paragraph_text": "OTC cough/cold medicines are not recommended for children younger than 6 years old and can result in serious and sometimes life-threatening side effects. But young children can have acetaminophen or ibuprofen for fever. Contact your healthcare provider about the correct dose and read and follow all directions.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > Children > p[15]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "b946b93b1d3cecc648762ce02fbf742bd68bb33f5bd61bd19d55bbeda4ac1b2b", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2825, 2901], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms", "Children"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 16, "paragraph_text": "Below are ways you can feel better while your body fights off cold symptoms:", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > Children > p[16]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "0ad151c72ca2982237450b742b69876fe54bf488cf1f904a412fdb50c1aa2ecf", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2902, 2948], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms", "Children"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 17, "paragraph_text": "Use a clean humidifier or cool mist vaporizer.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > Children > p[17]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "200c9ad0747824e2363103e1f6f92bc5073d0d758f8e0bdc6b7576d8472b85fb", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2949, 2981], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms", "Children"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 18, "paragraph_text": "Use saline nasal spray or drops.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > Children > p[18]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "0b07f87c77fd1eeb8b531576946180e6ce111f8374404cc47b37ddc2989e3dba", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2982, 3043], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms", "Children"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 19, "paragraph_text": "For young children, use a rubber suction bulb to clear mucus.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > Children > p[19]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "b745ae41d2294144c2310884edc008ff505a78a887279b89400d1a93cd2ed771", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [3044, 3096], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms", "Children"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 20, "paragraph_text": "Breathe in steam from a bowl of hot water or shower.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > Children > p[20]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "4ffb2f49a66af4f5d70d916995078d265969cf8483e982c8c6998bf8ab37b993", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [3097, 3167], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms", "Children"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 21, "paragraph_text": "Sit with a young child in a bathroom with steam from a running shower.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > Children > p[21]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "e3437069d6c1b997af1c26d592e90170dcebef5f67d8feebb5ff92d0dc96d320", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [3168, 3203], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms", "Children"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 22, "paragraph_text": "Use throat lozenges or cough drops.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > Children > p[22]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "291d5c6ecf6456b3c8e625f365c5e1236e77f833eac55624242917d93b7adfcd", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [3204, 3262], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms", "Children"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 23, "paragraph_text": "Do not give lozenges to children younger than 4 years old.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > Children > p[23]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "c5e7320994023725c979f205ba51bd1e3694271bd2de20478bdedc2ce02f3776", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [3263, 3334], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:44Z", "heading_path": ["Manage Common Cold", "Manage symptoms", "Children"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 24, "paragraph_text": "Use honey to relieve cough for adults and children at least 1 year old.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Manage Common Cold > Manage symptoms > Children > p[24]", "sha256_of_page": "4be1460cd86fb4aed6b8b6ec79feb0616e3b838b3be8b0169933d0c28dbb22bd", "sha256_of_paragraph": "e2f74b1dcfa6dfaf7a6c1016958d0090e53b1475deeebb97b93fe3b0ba3f2802", "source_id": "CDC-COLD", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/common-cold/treatment/index.html"}
