{"char_offset": [7508, 7792], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:48:53Z", "heading_path": ["Measles, Mumps, Rubella (MMR) Vaccine Safety", "How CDC monitors vaccine safety"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 35, "paragraph_text": "CDC and the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) are committed to ensuring that vaccines provided to the public are safe and effective. Once vaccines are licensed or authorized for emergency use in the United States, CDC and FDA continuously monitor them through several safety systems.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Measles, Mumps, Rubella (MMR) Vaccine Safety > How CDC monitors vaccine safety > p[35]", "sha256_of_page": "8545825cdf49ace4e7d502920e4a22a289cc3c07fa840bb2bdcc7a99ce6240b0", "sha256_of_paragraph": "c6f9d84537fe818b5503e537510297fecf249ae6421b6c7eab1eb998b54560cf", "source_id": "CDC-MMR", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/vaccine-safety/vaccines/mmr.html"}
