{"char_offset": [11449, 11570], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "What containers and wraps are safe to use in the microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 100, "paragraph_text": "Wax paper, parchment paper, heavy plastic wrap. Do not allow plastic wrap to touch food; vent it to allow a steam escape.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > What containers and wraps are safe to use in the microwave oven? > p[100]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "276d8a452fe8c38b21cf5b689e5426d15001e2d385db56e5a9aff5528ad246d3", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
