{"char_offset": [11937, 11978], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "What containers and wraps are safe to use in the microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 107, "paragraph_text": "Food completely wrapped in aluminum foil.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > What containers and wraps are safe to use in the microwave oven? > p[107]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "a221cd1472c4461191c6c9be37a21f29714612532474f88f6a156fbca708935e", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [11979, 12062], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "What containers and wraps are safe to use in the microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 108, "paragraph_text": "Food cooked in any container or packaging that has warped or melted during heating.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > What containers and wraps are safe to use in the microwave oven? > p[108]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "8304da3d8b2aa519a378bb32bd7e551eeff34df2a879bd50b7e93c324ef9a230", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [12063, 12267], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 109, "paragraph_text": "Always consult the owner's manual of your microwave oven and heed the manufacturer's recommendations for the use of aluminum foil. It can be safe to use small amounts of aluminum foil in a microwave oven.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven? > p[109]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "49e840441e4864d28a4674c500b7967b4fca14341b319a07e8999475eaa5ede9", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [12268, 12630], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 110, "paragraph_text": "Microwaves cannot pass through metal but are absorbed by food. No food completely covered by aluminum foil or in a covered metal pan should be put in a microwave oven because food wouldn't be available to absorb the microwaves. Operating the oven empty or when the food is completely wrapped in aluminum foil can cause damage to the oven and the food won't heat.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven? > p[110]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "3e1e44422dafcc4a283a92b6b969a07a238235c263baaecaca39b64848b108bb", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [12631, 12771], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 111, "paragraph_text": "However, small pieces of aluminum foil can be used to \"shield\" areas of foods, such as poultry drumsticks and wings, to prevent overcooking.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven? > p[111]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "6f7327fa3086296f68a07878d044abaa8cf4e0b5a7967c4a18c5c541974f0907", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [12772, 13169], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 112, "paragraph_text": "Some food packaged in foil containers can be safe to microwave. Read the package heating instructions to see if the food manufacturer has specific recommendations for microwaving the product. Because food in these containers will only heat from the top, it's best to microwave foods only 1-2 inches in depth so food near the bottom will be heated thoroughly before food on top dries and overcooks.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven? > p[112]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "e623e943adbdd36453bfb62edc031e1b361903208e3399e86fa7d141d3597ac4", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [13170, 13237], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven?", "General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil:"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 113, "paragraph_text": "Use new, smooth foil only. Wrinkled foil can cause arcing (sparks).", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven? > General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil: > p[113]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "19b8dcbe2482bb4741f0215b4ae96c4ef533b734caf324bc96822aac38b4b158", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [13238, 13283], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven?", "General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil:"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 114, "paragraph_text": "Cover no more than 1/4 of the food with foil.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven? > General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil: > p[114]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "1bc31aa3819bd2f548b5a99f748b0980a33bd3fa6ce11cba7e23f14ab4e777dc", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [13284, 13342], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven?", "General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil:"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 115, "paragraph_text": "Shape the foil smoothly to the food so no edges stick out.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven? > General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil: > p[115]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "248a300418505fa0423e54cef44a52fe413b5a3c990fea7c478beb8288897a73", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [13343, 13415], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven?", "General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil:"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 116, "paragraph_text": "It makes no difference which side of foil (shiny or dull) is facing out.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven? > General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil: > p[116]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "ff4ca33adba808b6bdc5fa5be8ee2b544a53ed73d84b41353c5b11ac0c53aaa4", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [13416, 13479], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven?", "General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil:"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 117, "paragraph_text": "Do not place the foil closer than one inch from the oven walls.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven? > General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil: > p[117]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "c369358c752b6a0e21f193ecd38f0a20ee24843af7be82cf77e34384374fd97a", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [13480, 13681], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven?", "General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil:"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 118, "paragraph_text": "If the microwave oven has metal shelves OR a metal turntable, don't microwave food in foil containers or metal pans, and don't let foil used for shielding touch or be close to the shelves or turntable.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven? > General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil: > p[118]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "9aa9c59fad014b0282d8d85b7c396be39612d5556b0ce4710fb514ac51d337cf", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [13682, 13818], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven?", "General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil:"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 119, "paragraph_text": "If you see arcing (sparks), immediately remove the foil shielding; transfer frozen food from foil container to a microwave-safe utensil.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Is it safe to use aluminum foil in a microwave oven? > General Rules for Safe Use of Aluminum Foil: > p[119]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "fe95c4ebb123c676e212ece806b21188ea86056fdebbc7e565be747525f33c51", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [13819, 13950], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How do you determine if a utensil is safe to use in a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 120, "paragraph_text": "If a utensil is not labeled for microwave use, you can test it before using to make sure it is microwave safe. Here's how to do it.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How do you determine if a utensil is safe to use in a microwave oven? > p[120]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "b6f977023cbd821f453c10de9250ba0f83b7a00bf533be89fad39eea7218b59d", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [13951, 14312], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How do you determine if a utensil is safe to use in a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 121, "paragraph_text": "Put one cup of tap water in a glass measure. Place the water in the microwave oven along with (but not touching) the utensil to be tested. Microwave on high 1 minute. If the utensil feels warm or hot, it is not microwave safe because it contains metal in the material or glaze. Do not use it. The utensil and/or the bottom of the oven might crack if microwaved.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How do you determine if a utensil is safe to use in a microwave oven? > p[121]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "4c71f42311ae5da627cd4608bd9d4f77d9c06cbc42ce3431f8b87158c4488f87", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [14313, 14505], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How does wattage affect microwave cooking?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 122, "paragraph_text": "The higher the wattage of a microwave oven, the faster it will cook food. So it's important for food safety to know the wattage of your oven when using cooking directions from various sources.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How does wattage affect microwave cooking? > p[122]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "c8a6535196408810db2c62510e635d314ba711c61ef968f61222d5eb59a487d9", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [14506, 14746], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How does wattage affect microwave cooking?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 123, "paragraph_text": "If you don't know the wattage of your microwave oven, try looking on the inside of the oven's door, on the serial number plate on the back of the oven, or in the owner's manual. You can also do a \"Time-to-Boil\" test to estimate the wattage.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How does wattage affect microwave cooking? > p[123]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "e625f1a16128ef7986f32c5c24e7c8ffacd4b441d03d1649c22a765e00b70547", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [14747, 14996], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How does wattage affect microwave cooking?", "\"Time-to-Boil Test\""], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 124, "paragraph_text": "Measure a cup of water in a 2-cup glass measure. Add ice cubes; stir until water is ice cold. Discard ice cubes and pour out any water more than 1 cup. Set the microwave on high 4 minutes, but watch the water through the window to see when it boils.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How does wattage affect microwave cooking? > \"Time-to-Boil Test\" > p[124]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "e50f7bf913cd9ba5de6ef7a7d6da575fd2bfe9d42c758f3dbddfe350773b7240", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [14997, 15086], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How does wattage affect microwave cooking?", "\"Time-to-Boil Test\""], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 125, "paragraph_text": "If water boils in less than 2 minutes, it is a very high wattage oven 1000 watts or more.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How does wattage affect microwave cooking? > \"Time-to-Boil Test\" > p[125]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "f1e188463235cb3e12b7baa9b992f0a139e1824fe30a84e8c2720b4327947c20", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [15087, 15167], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How does wattage affect microwave cooking?", "\"Time-to-Boil Test\""], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 126, "paragraph_text": "If water boils in 2½ minutes, it is a high wattage oven about 800 watts or more.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How does wattage affect microwave cooking? > \"Time-to-Boil Test\" > p[126]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "8858cc24ff4c65e51a0a4893fa0119e0ce84b85b876b9263b5ab4830598d5c72", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [15168, 15252], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How does wattage affect microwave cooking?", "\"Time-to-Boil Test\""], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 127, "paragraph_text": "If water boils in 3 minutes, it is an average wattage oven 650 to 700 watts or more.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How does wattage affect microwave cooking? > \"Time-to-Boil Test\" > p[127]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "8c50e25f1f7414c69a9b7f4cac8854ac62c7eb11f3f6e6a6c7d9183630811eb6", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [15253, 15347], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How does wattage affect microwave cooking?", "\"Time-to-Boil Test\""], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 128, "paragraph_text": "If water boils in more than 3 minutes or not by 4 minutes, it is a slow oven 300 to 500 watts.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How does wattage affect microwave cooking? > \"Time-to-Boil Test\" > p[128]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "07cbaaa8344123ed07932df8572d5261b27c82db426f64b0ebaafa4079571bb0", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [15348, 15523], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How does wattage affect microwave cooking?", "\"Time-to-Boil Test\""], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 129, "paragraph_text": "Use the minimum cooking time given for high wattage ovens; use the maximum cooking time for slow ovens. The minimum cooking time may need to be reduced for very high wattages.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How does wattage affect microwave cooking? > \"Time-to-Boil Test\" > p[129]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "bc30f200239da8a050e3144119b40c112ad74cbccbe707d49677ce986605a422", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [15524, 15769], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Do microwaves make food \"radioactive\"?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 130, "paragraph_text": "No. Microwave energy uses a wave length similar to television, radio waves, electric shavers and radar. It does not make food \"radioactive.\" X-rays and nuclear radiation are at the other end of the spectrum and are a million times more powerful.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Do microwaves make food \"radioactive\"? > p[130]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "cff1a7611ef961811534f60b42d25b6d9f67b80140b352dffcee7c8aa653e2c9", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [15770, 16046], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "Can a microwave oven be used for home canning?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 131, "paragraph_text": "Do not use the microwave for home canning or sterilizing jars. Use a water-bath or pressure canner, and approved canning jars and lids. At one time, \"canners\" were developed for use in the microwave; however these did not produce a safe product and are no longer manufactured.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > Can a microwave oven be used for home canning? > p[131]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "a6db5e42c4c5b1ef37b688b8885256b756f253d478a4a1f56714cb8355ae9923", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [16047, 16759], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "What is \"arcing\"?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 132, "paragraph_text": "Arcing (pronounced \"AR-king\") is sparks inside the microwave oven caused when microwaves react to gold paint on dishes, twist ties and other metallic materials. Some foods such as raw carrots and hot dogs can cause arcing while being microwaved. In hot dogs, this can be due to the uneven mixing of salts and additives. In carrots, it can be due to the minerals in the soil in which they were grown. Whatever the cause, turn off the oven immediately to end the sparks. Prolonged arcing can damage the oven and/or the utensil. If caught at once, arcing should not damage the oven. Remove the offending utensil or food from the oven and either substitute a microwave-safe utensil or cook the food by other methods.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > What is \"arcing\"? > p[132]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "c339cd9bf27dfa238019784b58a7001c0d3be5a030755572f9dfa9cde2fa8bf2", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [16760, 17250], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "What is \"erupting\"?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 133, "paragraph_text": "Erupting, or violent boiling over, can occur when a liquid (primarily water) heated in a microwave oven becomes hotter than its conventional 212 °F boiling temperature (super-heated). The liquid boils over when instant coffee, tea or gelatin is added to the superheated water. In extremely rare instances, all that is needed to initiate boiling of a superheated liquid is motion. Thus, a superheated cup of water could theoretically erupt violently when it is removed from a microwave oven.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > What is \"erupting\"? > p[133]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "2dbacae6e2672ff76d15dca5df59bb69e6b4d7432178642bc3ce1e47f10a0aaa", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [17251, 17586], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "What is \"erupting\"?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 134, "paragraph_text": "Superheating usually occurs when microwaving water in a very clean vessel — usually just taken from a dishwasher — or when microwaving room temperature water. It also happens because liquids heat with internal \"hot spots\" so that a temperature higher than 212 °F (the boiling point of water) builds up an inch or two below the surface.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > What is \"erupting\"? > p[134]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "cff3c55bd26f20624f1da7308209aead05b3a3bee8e6b6c7a3e8c834a2f3d1ea", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [17587, 17747], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "What is \"erupting\"?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 135, "paragraph_text": "Thus, even though it is extremely unlikely for an eruption to occur in a microwave oven, several precautions can be taken to lessen the potential for a problem:", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > What is \"erupting\"? > p[135]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "7ec79a993c7526e52c07b9ebe21957089ab46c3e196cda0678fece84924b3304", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [17748, 17805], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "What is \"erupting\"?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 136, "paragraph_text": "Use a vessel with sloping walls, such as a measuring cup.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > What is \"erupting\"? > p[136]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "2cf9fa46a6268d4d7a5a015b01c6daaedacadd412bf1ab7b25a16d4aed73f859", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [17806, 17861], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "What is \"erupting\"?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 137, "paragraph_text": "Leave a microwavable spoon in the vessel while heating.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > What is \"erupting\"? > p[137]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "d557090430b3af29bd05b885698f620384c88b2a3e5c348d1997a5b0a4da22d7", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [17862, 17894], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "What is \"erupting\"?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 138, "paragraph_text": "Stir occasionally while heating.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > What is \"erupting\"? > p[138]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "bf1ba3662f94a9d65a257a4aa342b5da81cb4d3c9a1a12aff2fa1e88633568bd", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [17895, 17992], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "What is \"erupting\"?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 139, "paragraph_text": "Add a pinch of instant coffee, a tea bag, or gelatin at the beginning or halfway through heating.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > What is \"erupting\"? > p[139]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "8e8c920c5c209e89bb863974e9daaaa225aaf26c288d0f4de67a722d63074d88", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [17993, 18280], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 140, "paragraph_text": "Consult the manufacturer's use and care manual for the best advice for your model of microwave oven. Some manufacturers recommend unplugging the microwave before cleaning it to minimize the possibility of electric shock. If you can't locate the manual, follow these general instructions.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven? > p[140]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "4ca207c76809709bdc16546584bfec5ebc6235de08675d7bcb424a10ed250bb3", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [18281, 18360], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 141, "paragraph_text": "Remove spatters and spills as they occur so food residue won't become dried on.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven? > p[141]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "3ed838b3832fab073cdb074839e251d8fea95581e5abcb5060872e39b0631d55", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [18361, 18430], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 142, "paragraph_text": "Wipe with a soft cloth or clean paper towel dampened with warm water.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven? > p[142]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "6a585cced8f8d74e5aed5c5603cae82278ea4cdef21ce4aff2de37ec6cec2ca9", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [18431, 18501], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 143, "paragraph_text": "For heavier soil, use baking soda, a mild soap, or dishwashing liquid.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven? > p[143]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "3ae70d08ca0b5b8f38a917d2c80dbac003cefed53949cac1f62134d871e283d8", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [18502, 18576], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 144, "paragraph_text": "Do not use steel wool, scouring pads, abrasive cleaners, or oven cleaners.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven? > p[144]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "5eaebc71eb08966dddbeab1007ad28745f6171a596f391ec247c1a5cab9f3331", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
{"char_offset": [18577, 18981], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:53:49Z", "heading_path": ["Cooking with Microwave Ovens", "How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven?"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "archived_copy", "paragraph_index": 145, "paragraph_text": "To remove food odors or loosen baked-on food residue, mix 6 tablespoons of baking soda OR 1/2 cup lemon juice with one cup of water in a microwave-safe glass measure. Microwave the mixture until it boils. Then leave the mixture in the microwave without opening the door until the mixture cools. The steam will help loosen food residue and remove odors. Wipe the surfaces with a soft cloth or paper towel.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "Cooking with Microwave Ovens > How should you clean the inside of a microwave oven? > p[145]", "sha256_of_page": "a3010e76a59170a0f610de828fd54011639e828730bad77e6f455bb1c995d19f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "9b3fb9808a0e56f8906e855263fb3d9eb7796bb29768abe8b3f8f5fffcbbb958", "source_id": "USDA-MW", "tag": "p", "url": "http://web.archive.org/web/20261119141358/https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/cooking-microwave-ovens"}
