{"char_offset": [6095, 6266], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:49:59Z", "heading_path": ["About Folic Acid", "Folic Acid"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 43, "paragraph_text": "Folic acid is a B vitamin. If a woman has enough folic acid in her body before and during pregnancy, it can help prevent major birth defects of the baby’s brain and spine.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Folic Acid > Folic Acid > p[43]", "sha256_of_page": "6cdc6c751cce000291222b2aafdadb124d38e8899d3cbddbfc5f0e8baa34158c", "sha256_of_paragraph": "6a23d1c4ffae6ea228ca3056ea7da6c88c08e063b109989818be54b92ad31eda", "source_id": "CDC-FOLIC", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/folic-acid/about/index.html"}
