{"char_offset": [414, 559], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "Key points"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 6, "paragraph_text": "Community water fluoridation is the process of adjusting the amount of fluoride in drinking water to a level recommended for preventing cavities.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > Key points > p[6]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "41176dabca99ab1597a0ed63c70ae0a2fcdf4c1e92b9f79517f6f1131d766b80", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [560, 713], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "Key points"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 7, "paragraph_text": "Community water fluoridation benefits all members of a community by preventing cavities, reducing oral health disparities, and saving money for everyone.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > Key points > p[7]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "bad65354d15910e79140d5d35b03e9cdeea58f44296b64eb6079139ec143c5e4", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [714, 862], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "Overview", "Notice‎"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 8, "paragraph_text": "CDC does not mandate community water fluoridation. The U.S. Public Health Service (USPHS) recommended fluoride level is not an enforceable standard.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > Overview > Notice‎ > p[8]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "b7bc99d61a5178906adfcc7e4d36cfa2f836d7f20b0b7e5edd9a8dfc4bb5a68d", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [863, 1107], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "Overview", "Notice‎"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 9, "paragraph_text": "Community water fluoridation is a cornerstone strategy for prevention of cavities in the U.S. It is a practical, cost-effective, and equitable way for communities to improve their residents’ oral health regardless of age, education, or income.1", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > Overview > Notice‎ > p[9]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "65411c6221f1d3a35f1dc4e0298bc690f6d65c01f72959f12b320fbdbf42da1d", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [1108, 1308], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "Overview", "Notice‎"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 10, "paragraph_text": "CDC named fluoridation of drinking water one of 10 great public health interventions of the 20th century because of the dramatic decline in cavities since community water fluoridation started in 1945.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > Overview > Notice‎ > p[10]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "a0713891456ac659c17f68d0e8224080a283a68ed6e68b7c0d43f76efdc0387d", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [1309, 1363], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "Overview", "Notice‎"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 11, "paragraph_text": "Keep Reading: Fast Facts: Community Water Fluoridation", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > Overview > Notice‎ > p[11]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "92e0e93ff9bd9bfc23f41ccfe1edeeb8d7c10dbc2e8c83030ca390227ce398d4", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [1364, 1678], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "How it works"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 12, "paragraph_text": "Almost all water contains some naturally occurring fluoride, but usually at levels too low to prevent cavities. The recommended fluoride concentration in drinking water (also called the optimal level) is 0.7 milligrams of fluoride per liter of water.2 This is about equal to 3 drops of water in a 55-gallon barrel.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > How it works > p[12]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "0be68cd35a70dd11aaca1e4e861cb0662b259901e3c0a892b0dd638db3e84281", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [1679, 2061], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "How it works"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 13, "paragraph_text": "State and local governments decide whether to implement water fluoridation. Often, voters themselves make the decision to adjust water fluoride to improve public health. Some states have laws that require water systems of a certain size to provide fluoridated water. In some areas, the level of naturally occurring fluoride in water is already at a level proven to prevent cavities.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > How it works > p[13]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "88da5e702c47f21403933ecd71c47cbdaa22a56dd3aa9d286f876e7e1756b624", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2062, 2209], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "How it works"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 14, "paragraph_text": "Community water systems add fluoride as needed to reach the optimal level. Communities also might remove fluoride if the natural level is too high.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > How it works > p[14]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "873f6498d6ce461c3af7a0b23b89c2f9e27f8d0fe12e33f690d555da5569559e", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2210, 2365], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "How it works"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 15, "paragraph_text": "Fluoridated water bathes teeth with a low level of fluoride throughout the day. This helps strengthen a tooth's surface, making it more resistant to decay.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > How it works > p[15]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "0372e72d7041ccade4ebb05ecbe2a76c3e9d047137855134adbe47ebcc2d3da9", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2366, 2604], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "How it works", "Did you know?‎"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 16, "paragraph_text": "Foods and beverages are often processed in communities that have fluoridated water. This extends the benefits of water fluoridation to people who live outside the community. This secondary benefit is called the halo (or diffusion) effect.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > How it works > Did you know?‎ > p[16]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "ed9ba4abc1ff11d45171efcaece07d328a23dc30ee892ed3ce37c073a1ab87b7", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2605, 2755], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "What the research shows"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 17, "paragraph_text": "Studies continue to show that widespread community water fluoridation prevents cavities and saves money, both for families and the health care system.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > What the research shows > p[17]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "8f0262117953878cff262942cff06c38f2f7e5fb08d00b6b3f217e7eeead6431", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2756, 2968], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "What the research shows"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 18, "paragraph_text": "Drinking fluoridated water keeps teeth strong and reduces cavities by about 25% in children and adults. 34This results in less mouth pain, fewer fillings or teeth pulled, and fewer missed days of work and school.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > What the research shows > p[18]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "cfa8b76c0e8cc801f4b608d623f2e63980ece402e8cef521377cd1ef4cd13b13", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
{"char_offset": [2969, 3347], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:24Z", "heading_path": ["About Community Water Fluoridation", "What the research shows"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 19, "paragraph_text": "Communities of 1,000 or more people see an average estimated return on investment (ROI) of $20 for every $1 spent on water fluoridation. The ROI for community water fluoridation increases as the community size increases, but even small communities save money.5 Communities served by fluoridated water save an average of $32 per person a year by avoiding treatment for cavities.5", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Community Water Fluoridation > What the research shows > p[19]", "sha256_of_page": "b3c326c193173006f89d383552e3796729d80343d96c33f61d7d8dc3e1d6a831", "sha256_of_paragraph": "906368403fc63bb975ff5f051fec4715ec4e7104c3e760cf478256584001a564", "source_id": "CDC-FLUORIDE", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/fluoridation/about/index.html"}
