{"char_offset": [760, 950], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:29Z", "heading_path": ["About Measles", "What it is", "For Healthcare Providers"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 10, "paragraph_text": "Some people think of measles as just a little rash and fever that clear up in a few days. But measles can cause serious health complications, especially in children younger than 5 years old.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Measles > What it is > For Healthcare Providers > p[10]", "sha256_of_page": "84a0c818aaaa7eaaff12f24e4ac658513097170bd019ebfe5277c3483df53747", "sha256_of_paragraph": "f501f2983a9c63340b7add3d60ec398a6741037440fc691e6f33125acbb3fe99", "source_id": "CDC-MEASLES-VAX", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/measles/about/"}
{"char_offset": [951, 1120], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:29Z", "heading_path": ["About Measles", "What it is", "For Healthcare Providers"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 11, "paragraph_text": "Measles is highly contagious. If one person has it, up to 9 out of 10 people who come into close contact with that person will become infected if they are not protected.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Measles > What it is > For Healthcare Providers > p[11]", "sha256_of_page": "84a0c818aaaa7eaaff12f24e4ac658513097170bd019ebfe5277c3483df53747", "sha256_of_paragraph": "bafc215c3bb2246b2bee3051809fa75d34727d71eb10e9dbfc466edda8597959", "source_id": "CDC-MEASLES-VAX", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/measles/about/"}
