{"char_offset": [1730, 2227], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:29Z", "heading_path": ["About Measles", "Who is at risk"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 18, "paragraph_text": "Measles was declared eliminated from the United States in 2000. However, since early 2025, U.S. measles cases have been increasing, and we've had several large outbreaks of more than 50 cases. Measles is also still common in many parts of the world. Every year, measles infections occur in the United States because unvaccinated travelers get measles while they are in other countries and then travel to the United States. These travelers are mostly Americans and sometimes international visitors.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Measles > Who is at risk > p[18]", "sha256_of_page": "84a0c818aaaa7eaaff12f24e4ac658513097170bd019ebfe5277c3483df53747", "sha256_of_paragraph": "60622396083a694cb165d59a04eae78eb45ef2f648bd6cf3809c809efbf548f0", "source_id": "CDC-MEASLES-VAX", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/measles/about/"}
