{"char_offset": [2532, 2774], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T12:50:29Z", "heading_path": ["About Measles", "How it spreads"], "language": "en-us", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 23, "paragraph_text": "Measles is very contagious. It spreads through the air when an infected person coughs or sneezes. You can get measles just by being in a room where a person with measles has been. This can happen even up to 2 hours after that person has left.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "About Measles > How it spreads > p[23]", "sha256_of_page": "84a0c818aaaa7eaaff12f24e4ac658513097170bd019ebfe5277c3483df53747", "sha256_of_paragraph": "6d2ea011063013fe48917a212bfcd494729788294357f8938aca36d70f7cb4e1", "source_id": "CDC-MEASLES-VAX", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/measles/about/"}
