{"char_offset": [112, 501], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T13:02:36Z", "heading_path": ["5 myths about the flu vaccine"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 2, "paragraph_text": "Fact: As many as 650 000 people a year can die of the flu. This only represents respiratory deaths, so the likely impact is even higher. Even healthy people can get the flu, but especially people whose immune systems are vulnerable. Most people will recover within a few weeks, but some can develop complications including sinus and ear infections, pneumonia, heart or brain inflammations.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "5 myths about the flu vaccine > p[2]", "sha256_of_page": "db5b60d626378d690f91b8ae49fcfc6015ec40d215a5c4d50959e3b9cdbc188f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "ebb7f0f1e5b72e295e8692c8298abbf09e9965c726b3c61406735b3e064cf605", "source_id": "WHO-FLU-5M", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine", "variant_of": "https://www.who.int/zh/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine", "variant_url": "https://www.who.int/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine"}
{"char_offset": [502, 545], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T13:02:36Z", "heading_path": ["5 myths about the flu vaccine"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 3, "paragraph_text": "Myth 2: The flu vaccine can give me the flu", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "5 myths about the flu vaccine > p[3]", "sha256_of_page": "db5b60d626378d690f91b8ae49fcfc6015ec40d215a5c4d50959e3b9cdbc188f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "f5bab00e4009b580421a7a80b2709cac0716ff20a685e30cf24fa972aafbe7cb", "source_id": "WHO-FLU-5M", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine", "variant_of": "https://www.who.int/zh/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine", "variant_url": "https://www.who.int/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine"}
{"char_offset": [546, 777], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T13:02:36Z", "heading_path": ["5 myths about the flu vaccine"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 4, "paragraph_text": "Fact: The injected flu vaccine contains an inactivated virus that cannot give you influenza. If you feel achy or slightly feverish, it is a normal reaction of the immune system to the vaccine, and generally lasts only a day or two.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "5 myths about the flu vaccine > p[4]", "sha256_of_page": "db5b60d626378d690f91b8ae49fcfc6015ec40d215a5c4d50959e3b9cdbc188f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "5a19536f0a46a35bdbfc1b6b41ab890b3a6da32c226abf76871d68029fe8eb98", "source_id": "WHO-FLU-5M", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine", "variant_of": "https://www.who.int/zh/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine", "variant_url": "https://www.who.int/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine"}
