{"char_offset": [1488, 1659], "fetched_at": "2026-11-20T13:02:36Z", "heading_path": ["5 myths about the flu vaccine"], "language": "en", "page_nature": "live", "paragraph_index": 10, "paragraph_text": "Fact: Pregnant women should especially get the flu vaccine since their immune systems are weaker than usual. The inactivated flu vaccine is safe at any stage of pregnancy.", "published_or_updated": "", "selector": "5 myths about the flu vaccine > p[10]", "sha256_of_page": "db5b60d626378d690f91b8ae49fcfc6015ec40d215a5c4d50959e3b9cdbc188f", "sha256_of_paragraph": "0931e56eff86be4ebf384a4a29fed5970f43e96084f6b508b473afd88fb0b426", "source_id": "WHO-FLU-5M", "tag": "p", "url": "https://www.who.int/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine", "variant_of": "https://www.who.int/zh/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine", "variant_url": "https://www.who.int/news-room/spotlight/influenza-are-we-ready/5-myths-about-the-flu-vaccine"}
